  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 1833b97b4e8284e489c3555d5dace838, type: 3}
  m_Name: PHP_TYPE_07_LOOPS
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CodeEscape.Programming.QuestionData
  id: PHP_TYPE_07_LOOPS
  language: 2
  topic: Loops
  difficulty: 0
  questionType: 2
  questionText: Type the part that adds 1 to $i after every turn of the loop.
  code: "<?php\nfor ($i = 1; $i <= 3; ____) {\n    echo $i;\n}"
  answerFormat: 1
  choices: []
  correctChoiceIndex: 0
  monospaceChoices: 0
  acceptedAnswers:
  - $i++
  - ++$i
  - $i += 1
  - $i = $i + 1
  caseSensitive: 1
  referenceFill: 
  runTests: []
  explanation: The third part of a for loop runs after each turn. $i++ adds 1 to
    $i, so the loop prints 123 and then stops when $i becomes 4.
  hint: You can add 1 to a variable with two plus signs.
  wrongChoiceFeedback: []
  wrongAnswerFeedback: Make $i go up by 1 each turn. Use the variable name $i with
    its dollar sign.
